# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): the engine agrees to 1e-12 relative in pe, c_p[1..6], press and the forces (1e-13 fails on c_virial[4] at 1.8e-13 relative).
# oracle: pair amoeba induced-dipole polarization (mutual solver, polarization energy c_p[5], forces and torques) with periodic images and no Ewald, on the AMOEBA water box (data.water_box.amoeba, boundary p p p, 216 waters) with the polarization test parameters w119amoeba_polar.prm (nonzero multipoles, alpha 0.837 and 0.496 A^3, Thole 0.39) and the cutoff 7 (taper 6) key w119amoeba_box.key; the buffered 14-7, permanent multipole and polarization terms are all included, every image within the cutoff counts.
# oracle-inputs: w119amoeba_box.data w119amoeba_polar.prm w119amoeba_box.key
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-12 abs=1e-10
units           real
boundary        p p p
atom_style      amoeba
bond_style      class2
angle_style     amoeba
dihedral_style  none
fix             amtype all property/atom i_amtype ghost yes
fix             extra all property/atom i_amgroup d_redID d_pval ghost yes
fix             extra2 all property/atom i_polaxe d2_xyzaxis 3
read_data       w119amoeba_box.data fix amtype NULL "Tinker Types"
special_bonds   lj/coul 0.5 0.5 0.5 one/five yes
pair_style      amoeba
pair_coeff      * * w119amoeba_polar.prm w119amoeba_box.key
compute         p all pair amoeba
compute         virial all pressure NULL virial
thermo_style    custom step pe evdwl c_p[1] c_p[2] c_p[3] c_p[4] c_p[5] c_p[6] press c_virial[1] c_virial[2] c_virial[3] c_virial[4] c_virial[5] c_virial[6]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             0
